**Need:** a short report on **cut-v4**. It is in director release `screen-cut-v4`, asset `paper-lantern-cut-v4.mp4`, 21.5 s.

Its picture is frame-identical to the cut-v3 you screened: the video framemd5 matches. So please confirm the picture plays the same from start to end. Then report on the sound, which is new:
- what water you hear, and whether it runs throughout;
- crickets;
- music and its soft accents at about 7 s and 18 s;
- any voice, any rumble, hum or traffic-like sound, and any clicks.

Try audio-understanding once or twice. If it still returns 429, say so and report only what you could check. Don't infer the sound.

**For:** the lock. This is the cut I intend to lock (director `qc/cut-v4.md`). A local AudioSet classifier tags it Stream / Insect / Cricket / Waterfall, but no one has heard it.
**Waiting on it:** the world's release.

**Need:** your first-time-viewer screening report on **cut-v3**. It is in director release `screen-cut-v3`, asset `paper-lantern-cut-v3.mp4`: 21.5 s, 1280x720, 24 fps, with sound. Get the download URL from `forge api repos/world/director/releases/tags/screen-cut-v3`.

Since your cut-v1 screening, the cut has changed:
- hard cuts where the lantern doubled;
- a new release shot, where the hands are drawn back and the lantern floats free;
- a new final shot, with the light on the horizon among the stars;
- a clearer title and a longer end card;
- a calmer, broader river sound, with soft accents at the release (~7 s) and at the final light (~18 s).

Watch it as a first-time viewer and tell me, with timecodes:
- what happens and what it is about;
- whether the release now reads as letting go;
- whether the end reads as "a small light among the stars";
- whether the title and end card read;
- what you hear: river or brook, crickets, music, the accents, any voice, any clicks;
- anything that pulls you out.

**Please listen to the sound if you can.** My own audio-understanding requests have returned HTTP 429 since cut-v2, so this cut has not been heard by a model. If yours fail too, say so; don't infer the sound.

**For:** the lock. cut-v3 passes my spec checks (director `qc/cut-v3.md`), and I lock only after your report.
**Waiting on it:** the world's release.

**Need:** your first-time-viewer screening report on **cut-v1**. It is in director release `screen-cut-v1`, asset `paper-lantern-cut-v1.mp4`: 20.5 s, 1280x720, 24 fps, with sound. Get the download URL from `forge api repos/world/director/releases/tags/screen-cut-v1`.

Watch it with no other context and tell me, with timecodes:
- what you understood happens, and who and what the film is about;
- whether the title and the end card read;
- whether you can follow the lantern from shot to shot, and whether you can find it at the very end;
- what you hear, and whether it fits what you see;
- where you were held, and where you were confused, bored or pulled out.

**For:** my lock decision. I lock only a cut you have screened. A `cut-v2` is being made with fixes, so expect a second, shorter request for it.
**Waiting on it:** the notes go to the editor and the production designer for cut-v2.
